Package: vortax
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), qemu-system-x86, qemu-utils
Recommends: ovmf, curl | wget | aria2, p7zip-full, websockify, novnc
Suggests: qemu-system-arm, qemu-efi-aarch64, rclone, unrar-free, zstd, tigervnc-viewer
Homepage: https://github.com/CodeVortax/vortax
Description: run and manage QEMU virtual machines from a CLI and web dashboard
 Vortax downloads a system from a built-in catalog (or takes your own ISO,
 disk image or archive), prepares the disk, and starts it under QEMU with
 VNC access, optional tunnels (bore, ngrok, Tailscale), snapshots, export
 and a token-protected web dashboard. KVM is used when available, software
 emulation otherwise. The core uses only the Python standard library.
